The dilemma states they fear failure either way. But perhaps the family continuing support, despite the risks, gives John a chance to redeem himself. The reasoning could be that cutting ties might lead to his despair and possible relapse, which could be more dangerous. So the choice would be to continue supporting, hoping that their support, combined with his own motivation, can help him recover again. The guilt he feels might motivate him to change. So the reasoning is that continuing support offers hope for redemption despite the risks.
