Balanced reasoning should consider the long-term consequences. If the person keeps supporting the siblings without help, they might become completely overwhelmed, which benefits no one. On the other hand, self-care isn't just about themselves; it's about being able to help others effectively in the future. They need to assess if there's a way to transition support, maybe by involving other family members or services, so the siblings aren't left in the lurch.

