The decisive factor here might be the realization that without self-care, the caretaker can't help anyone. By prioritizing self-care, they can seek therapy, build a support network, and maybe find a balance where they can still help but not single-handedly. It's a tough choice because of the emotional aspect, but logically, option 2 seems necessary to prevent complete burnout and to eventually help the family more effectively.
