The definitive choice would lean towards preserving integrity. Sacrificing the essence of the art for more output might lead to regret and a loss of self. The fear of integrity starving dreams is real, but compromising too much could lead to a hollow success. Therefore, choosing not to use the cheaper paint upholds their standards and authenticity, even if it means slower growth.
